1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,633
<i>Are they going to the carnival?</i>

2
00:00:01,767 --> 00:00:03,000
<i> Come on, let's follow them.</i>

3
00:00:03,133 --> 00:00:04,900
<i> Jin Ho, are you okay?</i>

4
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:06,700
<i> Yeah, I'm okay.</i>

5
00:00:06,833 --> 00:00:08,133
<i>Do you think
I didn't notice you?</i>

6
00:00:08,267 --> 00:00:09,700
<i>Do you want me to kill you
both here?</i>

7
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:10,767
<i> Why are you following me?</i>

8
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:12,900
<i>You left this at the eatery
earlier.</i>

9
00:00:13,033 --> 00:00:15,200
<i>That's my girlfriend's.
Don't follow me!</i>

10
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,000
<i>She's really going to take us
to Golda's.</i>

11
00:00:17,133 --> 00:00:19,100
<i>They might be staying there
overnight.</i>

12
00:00:19,233 --> 00:00:21,767
<i>I'll stay here, and you guys
go home.</i>

13
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,533
<i>How can I sleep?
Jin Ho hasn't come home yet.</i>

14
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:26,467
<i>Why are you so concerned
about Jin Ho?</i>

15
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:27,833
<i>You should only be worrying
about me.</i>

16
00:00:27,967 --> 00:00:29,567
<i> Wow, clingy?</i>

17
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,900
<i>Fine, you can say I'm clingy!
Well, what can I do? I love you!</i>

18
00:00:32,033 --> 00:00:33,600
<i> You love me? What's that?</i>

19
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:35,200
<i> You're my best friend, right?</i>

20
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:36,333
<i> That's why I love you.</i>

21
00:00:36,467 --> 00:00:37,700
<i> Andrew,</i>

22
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:40,467
<i>my friend replied about the
plate number you're checking.</i>

23
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:41,933
<i> Who is this registered to?</i>

24
00:00:42,067 --> 00:00:43,367
<i> Vicente Alcala's.</i>

25
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,333
<i>He's the biggest supplier of
ammunition in the Philippines.</i>

26
00:00:46,467 --> 00:00:50,567
<i>That's the M14 and AK-47.
That's for a special client.</i>

27
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:52,700
<i>This is where you're hiding,
Golda.</i>

28
00:00:52,833 --> 00:00:54,633
<i>Wow, you're really doing
a good job.</i>

29
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:56,633
<i> That's a big deal for us.</i>

30
00:00:56,767 --> 00:00:59,333
<i>Be careful.
This is a big syndicate.</i>

31
00:00:59,467 --> 00:01:02,033
<i>And with Joey, you take care
of her first.</i>

32
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,133
She hid with another syndicate.

33
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:26,567
She used her brains.

34
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:28,500
What's the plan?

35
00:01:28,633 --> 00:01:32,567
We'll wait for her to come out,
then we'll intercept her?

36
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:34,200
If we just wait for her,

37
00:01:34,333 --> 00:01:37,000
there's no guarantee
when we'll find her.

38
00:01:37,133 --> 00:01:39,600
But we're still pursuing her,
right?

39
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:41,767
We can't give up,
especially now.

40
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:43,600
We know where she's hiding.

41
00:01:43,733 --> 00:01:45,900
Well, it looks like we have
no other choice

42
00:01:46,033 --> 00:01:48,167
but to enter Godfather's villa.

43
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:49,867
It's dangerous.

44
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:50,900
For sure,

45
00:01:51,033 --> 00:01:53,067
his place is surrounded
by his private army.

46
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,733
We don't have any other choice.

47
00:01:54,867 --> 00:01:57,967
We have to be creative
to get access.

48
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,733
Yeah, but how?

49
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:02,000
The question is how!

50
00:02:02,133 --> 00:02:03,833
Are you mad at me?

51
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,433
No!

52
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:15,267
<i> Really?</i>

53
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,000
Okay, Becky, okay.

54
00:02:17,133 --> 00:02:18,300
Thank you.

55
00:02:18,433 --> 00:02:21,433
I'll come up with a proposal,
and I'll e-mail it to you, okay?

56
00:02:21,567 --> 00:02:23,867
Okay, thank you, thank you.

57
00:02:26,367 --> 00:02:29,800
Ma'am, it looks like
we have good news.

58
00:02:29,933 --> 00:02:32,367
Very good news, Clarissa.

59
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:37,167
Not just for me but for
the people we're helping.

60
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:39,367
Because I'm trying to look
for a sponsor

61
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:43,433
to support our monthly feeding
program

62
00:02:43,567 --> 00:02:45,933
and a friend of mine is trying
to connect me

63
00:02:46,067 --> 00:02:48,200
with someone who just might
say yes.

64
00:02:48,367 --> 00:02:51,200
I'll just fix the proposal,
okay?

65
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:52,333
Ma'am...

66
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:56,700
Can I talk to you?

67
00:02:56,833 --> 00:03:00,867
This is just about your offer
to me before...

68
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,967
about my husband's case.

69
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,733
Of course. What about it?

70
00:03:06,867 --> 00:03:11,733
I really want to ask
for your husband's help.

71
00:03:11,867 --> 00:03:16,600
Yes, the offer still stands,
so let's do it.

72
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:20,233
Let's sit down later and talk
about your husband's case.

73
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,367
So I can tell my husband too.

74
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,267
Is that okay?

75
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,767
Yes, thank you.

76
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,900
- Thank you very much.
- You're welcome.

77
00:03:31,667 --> 00:03:32,933
<i> The gate is too high.</i>

78
00:03:33,067 --> 00:03:35,933
There's no way from here.

79
00:03:36,067 --> 00:03:38,933
But there's a tree
on the other side.

80
00:03:39,067 --> 00:03:42,133
That's the perfect vantage
point.

81
00:03:42,267 --> 00:03:43,833
But the problem...

82
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,333
Hey.

83
00:03:47,467 --> 00:03:49,067
Stupid.

84
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,133
You stupid.

85
00:03:51,267 --> 00:03:52,400
What?

86
00:03:54,933 --> 00:03:56,167
You're mad.

87
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:58,633
I know, you're mad.

88
00:03:58,767 --> 00:04:00,333
I knew it. So tell me why.

89
00:04:00,467 --> 00:04:03,567
We can't pull this mission off
if you're acting like this!

90
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:10,467
I mean, you might as well
go home

91
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,400
and just let me handle it
myself, okay?

92
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,133
Smile, smile.

93
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:21,933
Hi. Sorry, I don't have anyone
to ask.

94
00:04:22,067 --> 00:04:24,200
I've been going around
for a while now.

95
00:04:24,333 --> 00:04:27,167
Do you know the house
of Vicente Alcala?

96
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,167
Sorry? Vicent...

97
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:31,633
Why, Miss? Why?

98
00:04:31,767 --> 00:04:33,833
Do you need anything
from our boss?

99
00:04:33,967 --> 00:04:35,967
You work wit him?

100
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,767
Well, it's a good thing.

101
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,633
The events team sent me.

102
00:04:39,767 --> 00:04:41,733
I'm the one who's going
to do the ocular

103
00:04:41,867 --> 00:04:43,967
for his house for his party.

104
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:45,533
Party...

105
00:04:45,667 --> 00:04:46,700
Yes.

106
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:52,967
Are you serious?

107
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:55,300
Did the event organizer
give you this?

108
00:04:55,433 --> 00:04:56,467
Yes.

109
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,567
You know, it's limited.

110
00:04:58,700 --> 00:04:59,833
But you know,

111
00:04:59,967 --> 00:05:02,133
we wouldn't have had that
if Jin Ho had made a mistake.

112
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:03,367
Right, Jin Ho?

113
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:06,833
Good thing I had a plan.

114
00:05:06,967 --> 00:05:09,033
This could be our way in,
actually.

115
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:13,967
What's important is that
we get the guest list,

116
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:16,067
then we can put our names on it.

117
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,833
Us?

118
00:05:17,967 --> 00:05:21,933
Joey, you're not included,
it's just the three of us.

119
00:05:25,767 --> 00:05:27,300
Why?

120
00:05:27,433 --> 00:05:31,000
Why are you telling me
what to do?

121
00:05:31,133 --> 00:05:35,667
Joey, it's dangerous,
and there's always a problem.

122
00:05:35,833 --> 00:05:38,067
Remember what happened to Golda?

123
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:40,167
What happened when you
showed up?

124
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:43,267
It got foiled, remember?

125
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,567
It's not good when there's
a girl around.

126
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:48,800
And one more thing,
you might get emotional.

127
00:05:48,933 --> 00:05:50,333
Wait a minute?

128
00:05:50,467 --> 00:05:52,067
What's your real issue with me?

129
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:54,367
Is it because I failed,
or because I'm emotional,

130
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:56,200
or because I'm a girl?

131
00:05:56,333 --> 00:05:58,733
What? Which one?

132
00:05:58,867 --> 00:06:01,567
Wait, where's that coming from?

133
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:04,033
I didn't say anything like that.

134
00:06:04,167 --> 00:06:06,367
Can you stop being so sensitive?

135
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,933
You just said it!

136
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:12,433
And please, I'm not the only one
who's sensitive!

137
00:06:12,567 --> 00:06:14,833
You're the one who is careless
with what you're saying!

138
00:06:14,967 --> 00:06:17,033
You're the one
who's insensitive!

139
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:20,600
Well, okay, if you don't want me
to come, then don't!

140
00:06:20,733 --> 00:06:23,600
I'll do my own thing.
I'll go alone.

141
00:06:31,867 --> 00:06:33,033
Great!

142
00:06:35,133 --> 00:06:36,000
Why?

143
00:06:36,133 --> 00:06:37,867
Is there something wrong
with what I said?

144
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,333
There's nothing wrong there,
right?

145
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:42,000
I have no idea.

146
00:06:59,767 --> 00:07:01,467
Joey, have some rice.

147
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,333
Eat first.

148
00:07:03,467 --> 00:07:05,167
Oh, no need, Peter.

149
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,300
Let me do it.

150
00:07:06,433 --> 00:07:10,300
I can handle it,
and just because I'm a girl,

151
00:07:10,433 --> 00:07:13,133
it doesn't mean I'm just
all emotions, right?

152
00:07:16,433 --> 00:07:18,933
What's with this chicken?

153
00:07:20,533 --> 00:07:25,533
I just want to eat,
but I'm just too sensitive.

154
00:07:25,667 --> 00:07:26,500
It's so tough...

155
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:27,733
Tough...

156
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,467
Tough.

157
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:35,067
You want water, Joey? Here.

158
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:40,400
Thank you, Jin Ho.
You're so sweet.

159
00:07:40,533 --> 00:07:42,667
You really care about
my feelings.

160
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:43,967
Thank you.

161
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:51,067
Be careful, Joey,
because you don't know...

162
00:07:51,233 --> 00:07:55,067
There are people who feel
like superheroes.

163
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,333
Wrong!

164
00:07:57,733 --> 00:07:59,200
Super wrong!

165
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:00,533
Do you know those mushrooms?

166
00:08:00,667 --> 00:08:02,100
The ones that appear,
appear, appear

167
00:08:02,233 --> 00:08:04,000
even though you don't need them.

168
00:08:04,133 --> 00:08:06,500
Are you talking about me?

169
00:08:06,633 --> 00:08:09,367
Why? Of course not.
Why would I talk about you?

170
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,767
Then why do you say it
in English,

171
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:12,133
so I can understand, right?

172
00:08:12,267 --> 00:08:13,533
What do you think?

173
00:08:13,667 --> 00:08:14,567
Are you guys fighting?

174
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:15,733
-No!
-No!

175
00:08:15,867 --> 00:08:17,133
Don't shoult.

176
00:08:17,267 --> 00:08:18,400
There's someone sensitive here.

177
00:08:18,533 --> 00:08:20,733
Be sensitive.
You might hurt someone.

178
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,067
It's up to you.

179
00:08:24,567 --> 00:08:29,500
That's right, you should analyze
the situation

180
00:08:29,633 --> 00:08:32,600
before you say anything.

181
00:08:32,733 --> 00:08:36,533
It's more important to analyze
your egos.

182
00:08:36,667 --> 00:08:37,300
So...

183
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:39,600
so, I have issues with my ego?

184
00:08:39,733 --> 00:08:41,533
Why? Were you hit?

185
00:08:41,667 --> 00:08:43,467
The chicken is so tough.

186
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:56,867
Hi, Hon!

187
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,000
The kids?

188
00:08:59,133 --> 00:09:00,967
They've eaten.

189
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:03,800
They're in the playroom
with Nanny.

190
00:09:05,167 --> 00:09:06,700
Hon...

191
00:09:08,433 --> 00:09:12,133
when's your Hong Kong
conference?

192
00:09:12,267 --> 00:09:15,167
This week. I'll be back
by Wednesday.

193
00:09:16,733 --> 00:09:18,800
Oh, so...

194
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:20,733
So, five days.

195
00:09:22,433 --> 00:09:25,267
I was just thinking,

196
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:29,967
if you could help me
with something, Hon?

197
00:09:30,133 --> 00:09:34,333
Well, it's about one
of my employees.

198
00:09:34,467 --> 00:09:40,400
Because her husband is in jail,
and they need assistance.

199
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:44,233
What kind of assistance?

200
00:09:44,367 --> 00:09:47,933
Well, I was thinking if
you could have someone,

201
00:09:48,067 --> 00:09:50,000
look into his case.

202
00:09:50,133 --> 00:09:54,800
You know, check if
he's eligible for bail

203
00:09:54,933 --> 00:09:57,700
or if there's anything
that can be done.

204
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,567
What's the case?

205
00:10:01,733 --> 00:10:02,967
Murder.

206
00:10:04,733 --> 00:10:08,400
His name is Miguel Delgado.

207
00:10:08,533 --> 00:10:12,233
Former Major Miguel Delgado.

208
00:10:12,367 --> 00:10:14,233
He used to be a police officer,
Hon.

209
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:19,900
I'll try to see what I can do.

210
00:10:20,033 --> 00:10:22,200
Okay, thank you.

211
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:36,267
Yo, yo, yo little brother.

212
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:39,500
What?

213
00:10:39,633 --> 00:10:41,267
Are you not drinking?

214
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:46,600
No, maybe you shouldn't,
cause you're still a baby.

215
00:10:46,733 --> 00:10:50,300
You know, you need to be
protected by...

216
00:10:51,967 --> 00:10:53,433
Superheroes!

217
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:55,900
Wow!

218
00:10:58,067 --> 00:10:59,667
Superhero.

219
00:11:00,967 --> 00:11:03,433
Okay, come here.

220
00:11:06,267 --> 00:11:07,867
We haven't started,
and you're drunk.

221
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:17,967
It's bitter.

222
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:20,033
You're still a baby.

223
00:11:28,133 --> 00:11:29,300
Delicious.

224
00:11:37,367 --> 00:11:39,100
I'll give you one more shot.

225
00:11:41,767 --> 00:11:43,233
You can do that.

226
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:52,367
- Andrew! Join us!
- Yes?

227
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:54,567
Yes! Come on.

228
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:57,600
Maybe you'll even be Superman
if you drink this.

229
00:11:57,733 --> 00:11:58,700
Fun!

230
00:11:58,833 --> 00:12:00,333
No, thank you. Pass, pass.

231
00:12:00,467 --> 00:12:01,633
I'm going to bed.

232
00:12:01,767 --> 00:12:04,200
- Hey...
- KJ.

233
00:12:04,333 --> 00:12:06,167
Yes, that's right.

234
00:12:06,300 --> 00:12:11,033
Alcohol is dangerous for robots
because they'll become rusty.

235
00:12:11,167 --> 00:12:13,367
They'll lose their feelings
even more.

236
00:12:20,633 --> 00:12:22,633
Game?

237
00:12:22,767 --> 00:12:23,800
What's this?

238
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:27,700
Soju.

239
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:42,333
Give me that.

240
00:12:44,433 --> 00:12:46,000
- Why?
- Are you drinking?

241
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:47,333
You react too much?

242
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:48,567
Why? What do you think?

243
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:51,100
I can't drink because
I'm a girl, right?

244
00:12:52,733 --> 00:12:54,100
You're a baby.

245
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:05,200
- What? Come on! Shot!
- Shot?

246
00:13:05,333 --> 00:13:07,433
- Shot!
- Shot?

247
00:13:07,567 --> 00:13:09,100
Wait, wait. Just take it slow.

248
00:13:09,233 --> 00:13:10,200
Shot!

249
00:13:19,533 --> 00:13:20,233
Bitter...

250
00:13:20,367 --> 00:13:22,800
- It's bitter!
- Look at this.

251
00:13:22,967 --> 00:13:25,400
She works for the Boss's wife.

252
00:13:25,533 --> 00:13:27,500
For how long?

253
00:13:27,633 --> 00:13:31,367
Yvette said it's been a month.

254
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:33,167
Isn't it dangerous, Boss?

255
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:37,000
Maybe she'll find out something
about the organization.

256
00:13:37,133 --> 00:13:39,100
What, should I work on it?

257
00:13:39,233 --> 00:13:40,767
No.

258
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:43,600
We have the upper hand.

259
00:13:43,733 --> 00:13:45,567
As long as she doesn't know,

260
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:48,667
we can use her against her
husband.

261
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,100
That's right.

262
00:13:50,233 --> 00:13:54,867
He'll suffer even more while
we're playing with his family.

263
00:13:57,067 --> 00:13:58,433
Exactly!

264
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:02,033
And that's how we burn him
slowly.

265
00:14:09,567 --> 00:14:10,467
No. I will show you
the real one.

266
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,767
- Go, go, go!
- All right!

267
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:13,200
Go, Jin Ho.

268
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:20,267
That's how...

269
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,733
Fix it!

270
00:14:23,833 --> 00:14:27,167
Joey! Joey! Come on, come on.

271
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,900
- Go, Joey!
- How? How?

272
00:14:39,767 --> 00:14:40,800
Wait.

273
00:14:40,933 --> 00:14:41,867
Yeah?

274
00:14:42,333 --> 00:14:44,167
You touched my heart.

275
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:45,500
I'm so touched.

276
00:14:45,633 --> 00:14:47,300
I want to cry.

277
00:14:47,433 --> 00:14:49,200
Okay, let's go. Next!

278
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:51,533
Next! Who's next?

279
00:14:51,667 --> 00:14:54,167
- Game, truth or dare?
- It's you!

280
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:01,267
You.

281
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,867
Truth or dare.

282
00:15:04,533 --> 00:15:05,933
Truth.

283
00:15:06,067 --> 00:15:08,333
- Okay, wait, wait.
- Truth.

284
00:15:08,467 --> 00:15:10,133
I have a question.

285
00:15:10,267 --> 00:15:12,533
What's your ideal man?

286
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,400
It's good if there is one.

287
00:15:19,933 --> 00:15:29,900
I like someone kind, loving,
gentle, and sweet.

288
00:15:30,733 --> 00:15:31,967
That's it.

289
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:34,700
Well, that's all me! That's me.

290
00:15:34,867 --> 00:15:36,533
- Really?
- Yes!

291
00:15:36,667 --> 00:15:39,433
- Crazy!
- How did it become you?

292
00:15:39,567 --> 00:15:44,400
I just don't like someone
arrogant, bossy,

293
00:15:44,533 --> 00:15:47,200
the one who thinks he's always
right,

294
00:15:47,333 --> 00:15:50,533
the one who's so insensitive.

295
00:15:50,667 --> 00:15:51,733
That's it...

296
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:56,100
someone with a heart of stone.
Yuck! It turns me off.

297
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:04,933
You know, it's good, Jin Ho,
you're not like that.

298
00:16:06,133 --> 00:16:07,133
Me?

299
00:16:08,733 --> 00:16:09,700
Yeah.

300
00:16:12,933 --> 00:16:14,367
I'm not like that.

301
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:18,067
Are you saying I'm your ideal
man?

302
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:20,900
I don't know. Maybe.

303
00:16:24,033 --> 00:16:25,533
I'll just go to the CR.

304
00:16:34,267 --> 00:16:37,067
I'll just go to the CRIS.
I'm just going to pee.

305
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,733
The CR is over here.

306
00:16:43,367 --> 00:16:45,100
He'll use the CRIS in the tree.

307
00:16:50,267 --> 00:16:51,800
<i> Vincent Alcala?</i>

308
00:16:51,933 --> 00:16:53,033
<i> Yes.</i>

309
00:16:53,167 --> 00:16:54,900
<i> Be careful.</i>

310
00:16:55,033 --> 00:16:56,800
<i> This is a big syndicate.</i>

311
00:16:56,933 --> 00:16:59,967
<i>And with Joey,
we know she's impulsive.</i>

312
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:02,067
<i> She won't easily give up.</i>

313
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:04,567
<i> You take care of her first.</i>

314
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:07,467
<i>Andrew, this guy won't respect
you.</i>

315
00:17:08,633 --> 00:17:12,467
<i> Guys, Trigger is here!
Let's continue our party-party!</i>

316
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,500
<i>Yes, it's a party-party
for real!</i>

317
00:17:14,633 --> 00:17:15,767
<i> Trigger!</i>

318
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:25,967
<i>Ramon Orbos, the cop they say
I killed, do you know him?</i>

319
00:17:42,633 --> 00:17:43,533
Buddy,

320
00:17:44,933 --> 00:17:47,333
can I ask you a favor?

321
00:17:47,467 --> 00:17:51,167
Can you set me up with him?

322
00:17:52,433 --> 00:17:55,000
Do you think he'll give you
time?

323
00:17:55,133 --> 00:17:57,367
Just because you're a cop
out there

324
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:59,200
doesn't mean you're important
here.

325
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:21,800
I'm drinking.

326
00:18:21,967 --> 00:18:23,433
Isn't it obvious?

327
00:18:25,433 --> 00:18:29,400
Can you just get out of my face?
Leave me alone. Go away.

328
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:31,767
You know what?

329
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:34,933
I really don't understand
why you're mad at me.

330
00:18:35,067 --> 00:18:37,967
- What did I do?
- That's the thing.

331
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:40,633
You're not doing anything!

332
00:18:40,767 --> 00:18:45,500
But Joey likes everything
you do.

333
00:18:45,633 --> 00:18:47,167
What's that?

334
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,267
Joey?

335
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:52,400
- Is it...
- Yes, it's about her!

336
00:18:52,533 --> 00:18:54,300
Everything about her!

337
00:18:54,433 --> 00:18:56,867
Because I like her, okay?

338
00:18:57,033 --> 00:18:59,233
But I'm unlucky, she likes you.

339
00:18:59,367 --> 00:19:03,167
What's funny?

340
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:07,033
- What's funny?
- Okay, listen.

341
00:19:07,167 --> 00:19:08,900
- What's funny?
- Listen!

342
00:19:09,033 --> 00:19:10,433
Joey's pretty, yeah?

343
00:19:10,567 --> 00:19:12,867
She's sweet and...

344
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,067
But you don't have
to worry about me.

345
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:18,300
To be honest, I'm not the one
you should be jealous of.

346
00:19:24,833 --> 00:19:27,933
You like her. I knew it.

347
00:19:33,333 --> 00:19:34,500
That's why.

348
00:19:42,267 --> 00:19:43,667
Last.

349
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:45,567
Wait, are you still drinking?
Hey, that's enough.

350
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:48,233
Joey, that's enough,
you're drunk.

351
00:19:48,367 --> 00:19:49,867
Why?

352
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,133
You're drunk, aren't you?
I said that's enough.

353
00:19:53,267 --> 00:19:55,033
You're drunk.
You're really hard-headed.

354
00:19:55,167 --> 00:19:55,867
Here you go again.

355
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,333
Why?

356
00:19:57,467 --> 00:19:58,633
Because...

357
00:19:58,767 --> 00:20:01,000
Because I'm a girl?

358
00:20:01,133 --> 00:20:03,800
That's what you're going to say.

359
00:20:03,967 --> 00:20:05,533
Look, you're drunk.

360
00:20:06,933 --> 00:20:08,967
I'm not drunk.

361
00:20:10,167 --> 00:20:14,000
You know, I didn't say anything
because you're a girl.

362
00:20:14,133 --> 00:20:18,467
What? Because I'm a kid?
Like that?

363
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:22,700
I'm not belittling you, okay?
So stop that.

364
00:20:22,833 --> 00:20:24,267
You're drunk. Go to sleep.

365
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:29,133
What do I have to do to make you
stop treating me like a child?

366
00:20:31,367 --> 00:20:32,933
Tell me!

367
00:20:46,267 --> 00:20:47,433
Go to sleep.

368
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,633
I said tell me!

369
00:21:22,967 --> 00:21:25,333
I talked to Trigger.
He agreed to what you wanted.

370
00:21:25,467 --> 00:21:28,400
What do you need from Trigger?
Are you going to ask for help?

371
00:21:28,533 --> 00:21:29,867
You're really fooling me,
aren't you?

372
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,500
Didn't we already talk
about this, Joey?

373
00:21:31,633 --> 00:21:32,433
You're not coming.

374
00:21:32,567 --> 00:21:33,733
What?

375
00:21:33,867 --> 00:21:35,233
Do you have a problem with me
being a woman again, right?

376
00:21:35,367 --> 00:21:38,133
I can fight too.
I'm a black belter.

377
00:21:38,267 --> 00:21:41,667
Remember, your enemies
are gun smugglers.

378
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:42,900
Good job!

379
00:21:43,067 --> 00:21:44,900
Maybe you've forgotten,
my father is a police officer.

380
00:21:45,033 --> 00:21:47,033
There's a party going on
at the Godfather's.

381
00:21:47,167 --> 00:21:49,033
It looks like the transaction
will happen there.

382
00:21:49,167 --> 00:21:50,700
Then, we need to get in.

383
00:21:50,833 --> 00:21:53,633
An invitation has arrived
from one of our target sponsors.

384
00:21:53,767 --> 00:21:56,567
We cannot miss this opportunity,
right?

385
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:59,500
The theme is The Great Gatsby.
I don't have anything to wear.

386
00:21:59,633 --> 00:22:00,667
We didn't prepare.

387
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,433
Costume? Wait.
